{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Enact a multi-millionaire wealth tax to fund research for ultra-rare diseases",
        "additional_details": "Many families of children with terminal conditions like Sanfilippo syndrome and BPAN have to fundraise millions themselves to finance research trials or foreign care. We believe a child\u2019s survival shouldn\u2019t depend on private fundraising.\r\n \r\nThe Government should create a ring-fenced fund administered by the NHS and UKRI to finance research and development, clinical trials and compassionate treatment access for ultra-rare diseases, which would be sustainably funded through a tax on UK-based individuals with net assets exceeding \u00a310 million.",
        "background": "Enact a wealth tax on multimillionaires and use the revenue to create a ring-fenced NHS and UKRI fund that would finance research, clinical trials and treatments for ultra-rare diseases.",
